    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106-a17">

                <pb facs="0257" n="201" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg201"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Liverpool</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-03-23"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 23,
                        1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: I have carefully perused your
                    memorandum as to the new regulations suggested by the board of trade regarding
                    fog-signals, and I must humbly beg to agree with them, having seen them working
                    very well on board the river steamers in New York. There has long been a want of
                    system, and in my humble opinion the proposed rules will be of great
                    service.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAS. DUCKWORTH,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Second Officer Steamship
                            Gaelic</hi>.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Messrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ismay, Imrie</hi> &amp; Co.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
